# API and security

- Authenticate every protected request.
- Verify workspace or tenant ownership server-side.
- Validate all external inputs.
- Keep secrets server-only.
- Return stable error codes and safe messages.
- Log enough context for diagnosis without logging secrets or sensitive payloads.
- Apply rate limiting or abuse controls to expensive endpoints.
- Use idempotency for generation, publishing, billing, and webhook operations.
- Time out external provider calls and handle retries deliberately.
- Do not swallow provider errors.
- Separate user-facing messages from internal diagnostic detail.
